Findings

The lab demonstrated that Linux group membership can be used to control administrative privileges.

The mlyons3 account was successfully configured as a sudo-enabled administrative user, while the standard account remained restricted.

The root account was configured with /usr/sbin/nologin, preventing normal interactive root login.

Lessons Learned

This lab provided practical experience with:

Linux user administration
Linux groups
File permissions
sudo configuration
Privileged access
Root account hardening
Principle of least privilege
Basic Linux security verification
